      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124331,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 17,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:17:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124332,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 17,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a predilection for the lower limbs {24087787}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:17:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124333,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 17,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with sharply delineated, solitary, erythematous or brown papules and nodules, measuring from 5&nbsp;mm to a few centimetres and occasionally showing a polypoid growth {24087787}. Dermoscopy reveals a linear or serpiginous vascular pattern with a string-of-pearls appearance against a homogeneous pale or pink background {29267474}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:17:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124334,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 17,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Middle-aged to elderly adults are most commonly affected, without a marked sex bias {24087787}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:17:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124335,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 17,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It is unclear whether clear cell acanthoma represents a benign neoplasm or an inflammatory/reactive dermatosis. The solitary nature, persistence, and lack of regression point to a neoplastic origin, but immunohistochemistry has demonstrated similarities in keratin expression with psoriasis {17667172; 7547383; 32989899}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:17:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124336,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 17,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:17:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124337,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 17,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:17:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124338,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 17,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Clear cell acanthomas are well circumscribed, with psoriasiform epidermal hyperplasia and elongated and fused rete ridges with thinning of the papillary plates and sparing of the adnexal structures. They are composed of keratinocytes with pale- to clear-staining cytoplasm, and there is an abrupt radial transition to adjacent normal keratinocytes. The pale keratinocytes contain PAS-positive glycogen. There is overlying parakeratosis and there are admixed intraepidermal and intracorneal neutrophils. The superficial dermis contains a mixed inflammatory infiltrate and prominent vasculature.</p>\r\n<p>Squamous cell carcinoma in&nbsp;situ can be separated by the presence of squamous dysplasia. Psoriasis is excluded clinically.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:17:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
